Step 1: Reverse the entire array (indices 0 to 4)

Array after Step 1: [5, 4, 3, 2, 1]

Step 2: Reverse the first k elements (indices 0 to 0)

Single element (index 0), no swaps needed.

Array after Step 2: [5, 4, 3, 2, 1]

Step 3: Reverse the remaining n-k elements (indices 1 to 4)

Array after Step 3: [5, 1, 2, 3, 4]

Final Output: [5, 1, 2, 3, 4]

## Solution
```java[]
class Solution {

     public void inPlaceReversal(int[] nums, int startIndex, int endIndex) {
        while(startIndex < endIndex) {
            int temp = nums[startIndex];
            nums[startIndex]  = nums[endIndex];
            nums[endIndex] = temp;
            startIndex++;
            endIndex--;
        }
    }

    public void rotateArrayByOne(int[] nums) {
        int rotateBy = 1;
        inPlaceReversal(nums, 0, nums.length - 1);
        inPlaceReversal(nums, 0, nums.length - 1 - rotateBy);
        inPlaceReversal(nums, nums.length - rotateBy, nums.length - 1);
    }
}
```

